+ *  - Indices 0, 1 and 2 are NOT tagged. They are stdin/stdout/stderr on every
+ *    thread by construction — the same underlying streams — so aliasing them
+ *    is the correct semantics, not a bug. It also keeps `write(1, ...)` and
+ *    `STDOUT_FILENO` working on a worker.
+ *  - The MAIN thread takes slot 0, so its fds are numerically identical to a
+ *    single-threaded build's. Only workers get large numbers. That is safe
+ *    here because wasi-libc's `fd_set` stores fd VALUES in an array rather
+ *    than indexing a bitmap by them, so `FD_SETSIZE` bounds the COUNT of fds
+ *    in a set, not their magnitude.
